<item><title>L’Archer chief calls for legal, finance and business reforms in Congo</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/l-archer-chief-calls-for-legal-finance-and-business-reforms-8e2ed6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/l-archer-chief-calls-for-legal-finance-and-business-reforms-8e2ed6/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>Gilles Tchamba says clear state rules, bolder entrepreneurs and finance that channels savings to businesses are needed for a healthier business climate.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:02:33 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" length="37606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Congo minister urges mindset reform to attract private investors</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-minister-urges-mindset-reform-to-attract-private-e01bd4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-minister-urges-mindset-reform-to-attract-private-e01bd4/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>Denis Christel Sassou Nguesso says administrative conduct is driving investors to seek more favourable conditions in other countries.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:58:59 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-minister-urges-mindset-reform-to-attract-private-e01bd4/share.jpg" length="42952" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-minister-urges-mindset-reform-to-attract-private-e01bd4/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Congo rights commission urges stronger support for violence survivors</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-rights-commission-urges-stronger-support-for-violence-7620a8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-rights-commission-urges-stronger-support-for-violence-7620a8/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>In a statement in Brazzaville, the commission called for better prevention and protection and an end to impunity for violence against women and girls.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:27:37 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" length="37606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
